1200 0 obj
<<
/Title (When an accident is detected and no user response is given within the delay period, the system assumes it is a real emergency.  It then sends an alert message with GPS location using the GSM module.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1202 0 R
/Next 1198 0 R
>>
endobj
1201 0 obj
<<
/Title (The MQ3 sensor measures alcohol level and compares it with a predefined threshold.  If the level exceeds the limit, the system locks the engine and displays status along with sensor readings on the LCD.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1199 0 R
/Next 1203 0 R
>>
endobj
1202 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system detects a potential accident and starts a delay timer for confirmation.  If the user presses the push button within the delay, the alert is cancelled to avoid false notification.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1204 0 R
/Next 1200 0 R
>>
endobj
1203 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system retrieves longitude coordinates from the GPS module to determine the exact position of the vehicle.  These coordinates are sent via GSM to provide precise location information in alert messages.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1201 0 R
/Next 1205 0 R
>>
endobj
1204 0 obj
<<
/Title (The accelerometer senses a sudden high impact indicating a possible accident condition.  A countdown timer is initiated, allowing the user to cancel the alert before automatic message transmission.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1205 0 R
/Next 1202 0 R
>>
endobj
